You may remember me posting a few weeks ago about the Wizard not
dropping the Book. Well, this is the best game I have ever had by far,
but I think it qualifies for YASD.

To recap: I was Marion-Bar-Fem-Hum-Cha at XL 19,  AC -17, with the +6
Cleaver and a lot of other goodies. I had just killed the Wizard
(blowing through a "oLS in the process, but I had three more) and
couldn't find the Book. The consensus was that he had read a cursed
?oT, putting him who knows where.

I climbed a few levels, thinking it might be a good idea to exchange
some of the 30k zm I had for a little extra protection. Not long into
this, I feel vaguely nervous. "Score!" I think, "The Wizard will find
me." He did, this time dropping the Book, and I go down to the VS and
perform the ritual.

I struggled to get into the Sanctum and kill the High Priest and I
think I lost another "oLS in the process. I killed Rodney one or two
more times before I got the Amulet and escaped.

As I was scaling back up, I had abysmal luck with Rodney. Once I killed
him only to have him reappear about ten turns later. (It wasn't his
clone -- he even gave the "So thou thought" speech again.) I ran
through all my /oDs in the process and subsequently my other two "oLS,
then I died at his hands. Final score: Marion 8, Rodney 5. Pity Rodney
gets infinite respawns.

So far this isn't a YASD. What makes it a YASD is that I didn't have
fire resistance. I was down to 134 max HP when I was finally killed,
where I should've had over 200. ;_;

Oh well. Lesson learned. I am now onto Lara-Arc-Fem-Dwa-Law, who had a
good protection run and is running -8 AC with horrible equips (so once
I get good stuff, she will go much lower), but who also managed to
stumble on a long sword named Fire Brand... I am feeling lucky once
more.



